From 364d3edcb497c323c48af252e6761428fc43bad9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:04:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: mdio: add CM-T43 pre-discovery PHY initialization

A PHY described only by a generic Clause 22 compatible must have its
identifier read over MDIO. fwnode_mdiobus_register_phy() performs that
read before phy_device_register(), while the existing reset GPIO handling
happens later from mdiobus_register_device(). Consequently a PHY which
requires its reset line to be driven cannot acknowledge the discovery
transaction. A model-specific ethernet-phy-id compatible hides the problem
because it lets phylib create the device without accessing the hardware.

Add fwnode_mdio_cmt_43.c for the CM-T43 pre-discovery reset sequence. Build
it with CONFIG_TI_DAVINCI_MDIO_CM_T43 and additionally gate it at runtime
with the compulab,cm-t43-phy-init property on the MDIO bus. This keeps the
board-specific behavior out of the generic fwnode implementation and leaves
other MDIO buses unchanged.

For CM-T43 PHY nodes whose ID must be discovered, acquire the optional reset
GPIO before get_phy_device(). Assert and deassert it using reset-assert-us
and reset-deassert-us, then retain the descriptor and transfer it to the
newly created mdio_device. Teach MDIO registration to reuse a pre-acquired
reset descriptor and clear GPIO/reset-controller pointers when the device is
unregistered so normal cleanup and error paths retain single ownership.

Move the remaining CM-T43 PHY reference-clock setup from direct
CONTROL_MODULE and PRCM register accesses to the common clock framework.
Describe the complete AM437x CLKOUT2 mux, divider and gate chain, and model
the EXTDEV DPLL M2 output gate separately from its divider. The separate
gate is required because DPLL_CLKOUT_GATE_CTRL bit 8 must remain asserted
for CLKOUT2; the former auto-idle description allowed that bit to be
cleared.

Extend the TI DPLL provider and its binding with opt-in ti,mn-bypass
support. CM-T43 advertises both MN-bypass and locked modes for DPLL_EXTDEV,
sets its M2 output to 2.5 MHz, and selects that output as the CLKOUT2 parent.
MN bypass is board-specific because low-power bypass does not provide the
PHY reference clock required by this hardware. Configure the
xdma_event_intr1 pad for CLKOUT2 and expose the resulting clock to the
DaVinci MDIO device as phy-ref.

Have the CM-T43 MDIO helper acquire and enable phy-ref through managed clock
framework APIs before PHY reset and discovery. Keep the clock enabled for
the MDIO device lifetime and retain the required 10 ms settling delay.

Describe both CM-T43 RTL8211E devices with the generic
ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22 compatible. Their IDs are obtained from addresses
4 and 5 through the normal fwnode discovery path instead of being supplied
by the device tree.

Tested on a CM-T43 with two RTL8211E PHYs. The driver enabled phy-ref at
2.5 MHz, detected both PHYs at addresses 4 and 5, attached the RTL8211E
driver, negotiated 1 Gbit/s full-duplex links, and obtained DHCP leases on
eth0 and eth1. The device-tree-supplied ethernet-phy-id001c.c915 compatible
works as well.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
